Third-party notices

1. "Claude" trademark
   "Claude" is a trademark of Anthropic PBC. Chronicle is an independent project
   and is NOT affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to Anthropic PBC. The
   name is used descriptively, to identify the assistant Chronicle observes on
   the operator's own machine, alongside the other coding tools it reads (Codex,
   Cursor, OpenCode). Each is the trademark of its respective holder and is used
   nominatively, never as a claim of partnership, sponsorship or endorsement.

2. Bundled runtime dependencies
   The published package depends on these libraries at runtime, all under the MIT
   license:
     - Express            https://expressjs.com/
     - js-yaml            https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml
     - three              https://threejs.org/
     - react-force-graph-3d  https://github.com/vasturiano/react-force-graph
   three and react-force-graph-3d back the Memory graph's 3D canvas and are
   loaded lazily. Everything else in the dependency tree is a build-time or
   test-time tool and is not distributed with the package. Chronicle bundles no
   web fonts (it uses the operating system's own UI and monospace faces) and no
   third-party icon set (its glyphs are original monospace characters).

3. Local-only data
   Chronicle never bundles, transmits, or commits the operator's machine data. It
   writes its imported-session database and app state to the app data directory
   (~/.chronicle by default, CHRONICLE_DATA_DIR override), which is gitignored,
   and reads source tool logs read-only. It reads no other tool's files. Only
   sanitized templates
   ship with the project: the example seeds (data/*.example.json) and wholly
   synthetic demo fixtures (data/*.demo.json, data/demo-logs/) whose every
   number, project and note name is invented.
